 "prompt": "This double piston extender works in vanilla Minecraft Java 26.3, but this server runs with changed physics: each repeater delay step lasts 1 game ticks (vanilla: 2, so delays 1-4 are 2/4/6/8 ticks). Adapt the build so it works here.\n\nGoal: Pushes the lime concrete block 2 cells east, from (2,0,0) to (4,0,0), when the lever is switched on, and brings it fully back to (2,0,0) when the lever is switched off.\n\nSpec (checked in the game engine):\n- Lever at [-1, -1, 4]; it starts off. The grader settles the build, then flips the lever 6 times (idle gaps [0, 3, 7, 1, 11, 2] ticks before each flip).\n- After each flip the build must come to rest within 60 ticks, then stay unchanged for 40 ticks.\n- Lever off (start and after every even flip): (2, 0, 0) is lime_concrete; (3..4, 0, 0) is air.\n- Lever on (after every odd flip): (4, 0, 0) is lime_concrete; (2, 0, 0) is sticky_piston or piston.\n- The whole build must return to exactly the same resting state every two flips; no item drops; no block may leave the box.\n- At most 33 blocks (lever included), all inside the box [-2, -3, -1]..[6, 2, 5].\n- Exactly 1 lime_concrete in the build, at all times.\n- These cells must stay empty at every tick: [[3, 1, 0], [3, -1, 0], [3, 0, 1], [3, 0, -1], [4, 1, 0], [4, -1, 0], [4, 0, 1], [4, 0, -1], [5, 1, 0], [5, -1, 0], [5, 0, 1], [5, 0, -1], [5, 0, 0]].\n\nYou may change, add or remove any blocks except the lever. Allowed blocks: the benchmark allow-list. Submit the complete build as a list of blocks.",
 "verified": true
}